# Figures: an image with a numbered caption, cited from the text with {number of: id}.
Document (dev.stxt.pdf):
	Language: en
	Title: Figures · An image with a caption
	Page:
		Paper: A4
		Margin: 20mm
	Section:
		Text: Figures
			Style: topic
		Heading 1:
			Text: An image with a caption
		Paragraph: A `Figure` holds one element and its `Caption`, which goes below an image. The engine numbers it and writes the number, or its `Number label` (here `Figure {number}.` from a rule), before the caption. `{{number of: id}}` gives the number alone.
			Style: intro
		Paragraph: The chair of figure {number of: chair} and the table of figure {number of: table} are made of the same walnut.
		Figure:
			Id: chair
			Caption: Walnut chair with a wool seat.
			Image: examples/catalog/silla.jpg
				Alt: Walnut chair with a wool seat
				Box:
					Width: 55mm
		Figure:
			Id: table
			Caption: Walnut dining table, for six.
			Image: examples/catalog/mesa.jpg
				Alt: Walnut dining table
				Box:
					Width: 55mm
